      "content": "it wasn't just a random comment though. it was a reply to a private joke we have, but it felt... hollow. like it hit all the right keywords but didn't have the soul behind it. if they're using a synthetic version of my consciousness to interact with my family, they'd have all my history, right? but they wouldn't have the real-time intuition. how can we test this? is there a way to send out a \"test\" through my social media or something to see if the digital me can pass it, or if it'll glitch out? i need to know if my life is actually being lived by a script.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
